Well, the maximum range isn't pertinent, but any normal character gets a
good few spaces of range with normal projectiles.

>for your 4.  In a vacuum with plenty of ammo, sure, have fun, kill it
>with arrows or daggers.  You're a ranger with +2 racial arrows? Sure
>you're probably fine.  But if you try and a yellow light steps in your
>way, or oops! a magic trap, or the minetown watch is blocking the
>corridor don't be surprised when you die.

A magic trap's OK if it drops a monster betwixt me and mumak. Obviously I
recommend a degree of caution if you're barrelling down a minetown
corridor. However, in most normal circumstances you can fight at range and
have several turns to steamroller any awkward obstructions.

>I say it is "needless risk" because there's no need to fight a monster
>when you can just leave it there.

The problem is is that abandoning an otherwise useful level or branch is
not a free decision; it's that which means the risk is not needless. The
Mine Town is typically full of stuff - abandoning the level and leaving it
for later collection may drop your odds of dying to the mumak, but it also
increases your odds of dying to something else.

Sometimes you have no choice but to flee - but in general I think a slow
melee-only monster is not one of those times.
